# a part of the day fused with TODAY, as English "tonight" is: "i" before a
# bare part-of-day noun names today's band.  "i nat" is "tonight" or "last
# night" (https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/i_nat); "i formiddag",
# "i eftermiddag" and "i aften" follow the same pattern, as Norwegian
# "i ettermiddag tar jeg fri" does (Bokmålsordboka, ettermiddag,
# https://ordbokene.no/bm/13299).
i formiddag
i eftermiddag
i aften
i nat
